kwin-effect-upscale (0.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Auto reaches every program it applies to. A starting Wayland program is
    told the smaller output mode when it binds wl_output, and one the
    announcement did not reach falls back to a fractional scale below one.
  * An experimental session proxy in front of Xwayland gives selected X11
    games smaller display information before their first window. KWin
    starts it from the next login on; it can be switched off in the
    settings.
  * Game settings inherit from All applications, whose methods now default
    to Auto. An inherited value is shown in italics, and a reset button
    returns a changed one to the value of All applications.
  * Native no longer refuses a window, and the heads-up shows the supplied
    size in red when a game draws at a size other than the one chosen.
  * The pointer, clicks and mouse look reach an X11 game across the whole
    upscaled picture, and an X11 fullscreen game is given its size before
    its first window is shown.
  * A game that stays at full size can be handed to an optional helper on
    the session bus. This package does not install one.
  * The catalogue recognizes Left 4 Dead 2 by its game folder, adds
    Wreckfest, and no longer pins the benchmarks to Native.

 -- Jens Koehler <kwin-effect-upscale@koehler-speyer.de>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:51:43 +0200

kwin-effect-upscale (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Every setting is a global default with an optional per-application
    override. The method is chosen per presentation - Wayland and X11,
    fullscreen, borderless and windowed - and Auto finds one by itself.
  * Applications are recognized by their program path and their window
    class and instance, each compared exactly, as a substring or as a
    regular expression.
  * The settings page is laid out as one form, and its application list
    can be reordered and shows which open windows an entry matches.
  * Settings stored by 0.1.0 snapshots are read under their old meaning
    and rewritten in the new form when the settings page is applied.
  * X11 resolution requests hold on KWin 6.6.

 -- Jens Koehler <kwin-effect-upscale@koehler-speyer.de>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 17:58:18 +0200

